==Enemy==
Mooth is a mid-ranged enemy with only one knockback, a fast attack rate, good speed and decently high stats. This often means he can push easily and prove to be difficult to fight off for newer players.

In [[Legend Stages]], Mooth's position as a threatening backline enemy is quickly stolen by [[Owlbrow]], an enemy who behaves similarly to Mooth but moves slower, deals substantially higher damage with a longer backswing. Mooths however are still common in later stages as a source of funding, thanks to his extremely high money drop.

==Strategy==
If you have trouble with Mooth, use [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cats]] and [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cats]] to stall him, then deploy strong attackers like [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Titan Cat]] or long-ranged cats like [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Lizard Cat]]. A good method to defeat Mooth is to overwhelm him with fast-hitting units, like [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Cow Cat]]. [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|Anti-Floating Cats]] or [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Swimmer Cat]] can be useful against him as well, more so if they can outrange him.

As mentioned before, Mooth becomes much less threatening as the player makes progress, and mainly acts as a money source (i.e. [[Draconian (Deadly)|Draconian]]) or a wall to not let meatshields pass due to having only one knockback. Beyond that, he's only relevant when paired with [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal Enemies]] such as in [[Blockchain Twilight]].

