==Trivia==
*Mooth's name may be a pun on ''moth'' and ''smooth'' (as in smooth wings or flying smoothly). It could also be derived from 喪男 (Internet slang for an unpopular man), which can be read as ''modan'' or less commonly ''mootoko'' or ''moo''.
*''Ga'' (ガ) can mean "moth", so Mooth's Japanese name, Gagagaga (ガガガガ), literally translates to "Moth" being repeated four times. Most of his variants follow a similar naming scheme as well:
**[[Othom]]'s Japanese name, Chō Chōchō (超町長), is a pun that doesn't translate well to English: ''chō'' (蝶) can mean "butterfly", but the way Othom's name is spelled literally translates to "Super Mayor".
***Othom's Japanese description also contains several other words with chō as part of their pronunciation, which totals up to 12 times if his name is also included.
**[[Sister Lione]]'s Japanese name, Shishi Shimai (獅子姉妹), repeats the syllable ''shi'' three times but uses a different kanji for each one, literally translating to "Lion Sister" and sounding much like 獅子舞 ''shishimai'' ([[wikipedia:Lion dance|lion dance]]).
**[[Mega-Mooth]]'s Japanese name, Gigagaga (ギガガガ), simply combines the prefix ''giga-'' with ''Gagagaga''.
*It is heavily implied that the Mooth in [[The Battle Cats]] is the son of the Mooth in [[Kumanchu Royale]]. The Battle Cats Mooth's Japanese description says he was hoping to become a beautiful butterfly in the future and was once a delinquent but eventually started reforming, while the Kumanchu Royale Mooth's description claims he was also a delinquent and wishes his child to become a beautiful butterfly in the future instead of living the same way as he did.
*He is the first [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemy encountered in-game, but not the first in terms of ID - that honor goes to [[The Face]], who has a lower ID than Mooth despite appearing later.
*Mooth and his variants all have the exact same delay between attacks, foreswing, and backswing.
*From [[Version 2.0 Update|Version 2.0]] to [[Version 5.9 Update|Version 5.9]], Mooth was a [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]]/Floating enemy.

